---
import ServicePage from '../../components/services/ServicePage.astro';

export const prerender = true;

const canonical = 'https://busqueneil.com/services/landing-pages';

const FAQ = [
  {
    q: 'How long does a landing page take?',
    a: 'Usually a few days from the first conversation to a live page, as long as you can answer questions about your offer and customers quickly. The build is rarely the slow part. Deciding what the page should actually say is.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you write the copy or do I?',
    a: "I write it. A landing page is mostly an argument, and the design only decides how easily that argument gets read. If you already have copy you're confident in, I'll build to it and tell you where I think it loses people.",
  },
  {
    q: 'What makes a landing page convert?',
    a: 'One page, one audience, one action. A specific promise rather than a generic one, proof near every claim that needs it, objections handled before the form instead of after, and a fast load on a phone. Most underperforming pages fail on specificity and speed long before they fail on design.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you run A/B tests on it?',
    a: "Yes, and I build the page so testing is possible from day one: the headline, hero and offer block can be swapped without a rebuild. Testing only pays off once you have enough traffic for a result to mean something, so I'll tell you if you're not there yet.",
  },
];
---
<ServicePage
  title="Landing Page Design That Converts | Neil Busque"
  description="One focused page built to convert the traffic you already pay for. Copy, design, build and tracking included. See the work, then send Neil Busque your offer."
  canonical={canonical}
  heading="Landing pages that **convert**."
  lead="One page, one audience, one obvious next step. Copy, design, build and tracking, so the traffic you already pay for stops leaking."
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/' },
    { name: 'Services', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/services' },
    { name: 'Landing Pages', url: canonical },
  ]}
  topic="landing pages"
  artSeed="landing-pages"
  artPalette="paper"
  summary={{
    items: [
      'A short research pass on your offer and buyer',
      'Copy written for the page',
      'A custom page, tested at real phone sizes',
      'Analytics and conversion tracking that work',
    ],
    facts: [
      { term: 'Good for', value: 'Paid traffic, a single offer or a new campaign' },
      { term: 'How it starts', value: 'Send me the offer and where the traffic comes from' },
      { term: 'What you own', value: 'The page, the copy and the code' },
    ],
  }}
  related={['funnel-builder-kits', 'ai-ads-app']}
  relatedPalettes={['mist', 'navy']}
  faq={FAQ}
  service={{
    name: 'Landing Page Design and Development',
    serviceType: ['Landing page design', 'Conversion rate optimization', 'Sales page copywriting', 'A/B testing'],
    areaServed: ['New Jersey', 'New York', 'New York City', 'United States', 'Remote'],
  }}
>
  <h2>When you need a landing page instead of a website</h2>
  <p>A website answers every question a visitor might have. A landing page answers exactly one, and removes everything else.</p>
  <p>You want a landing page when you send paid traffic somewhere, launch one offer, test a new market or collect leads for a specific campaign. Sending ad traffic to a home page is the most common way I see a budget quietly wasted: the home page has to serve everyone, so it convinces no one in particular.</p>

  <h2>What actually moves the number</h2>
  <p>After building these for clients and for my own products, the same few things decide it, and design is further down the list than people expect.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Specificity.</strong> "Cut your onboarding from 30 days to 7" beats "streamline your workflow." One is a claim you can argue with. The other is wallpaper.</li>
    <li><strong>Proof next to the claim.</strong> Not a testimonial wall at the bottom that nobody scrolls to. Evidence beside the sentence that needs it.</li>
    <li><strong>Objections handled before the form.</strong> Every unanswered doubt becomes a closed tab: price, timeline, "will this work for my situation," lock-in.</li>
    <li><strong>Speed on a phone.</strong> Most paid traffic is mobile. A page that takes five seconds has already lost a chunk of the people you paid for.</li>
    <li><strong>One action.</strong> A second competing call to action reliably lowers both.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What the build includes</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>A short research pass.</strong> Your offer, your buyer and what competitors already promise, so the page doesn't repeat the category's wallpaper.</li>
    <li><strong>Copy written for the page.</strong> Headline, subhead, body, objections and calls to action as one argument, not sections filled in.</li>
    <li><strong>A custom-built page.</strong> Fast, responsive and tested at real phone sizes before it goes live.</li>
    <li><strong>Tracking that works.</strong> Analytics and conversion events wired up, so you can tell what happened instead of guessing.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Check your page first</h2>
  <p>I built a <a href="/analyzer">free landing page analyzer</a> because I kept running the same check by hand. It scores any page for speed, mobile and conversion, and can email you a full report. Run it against the page you have before you talk to me.</p>
  <p>That's the honest order: find out whether your current page is the problem before paying anyone to replace it. If the page is only one piece, read about <a href="/services/funnels">the full funnel</a> or <a href="/services/websites">websites</a>.</p>
</ServicePage>
